WEBVTT

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:19.937
<i>Kristin: hey, meredith, it's kristin.</i>

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.137
<i>You have to tell me
what happened last night.</i>

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:23.137
<i>Call me.</i>

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:26.471
<i>Brad: hey, meredith. Brad calling.</i>

00:03:26.504 --> 00:03:29.304
<i>Listen, do you want to hook up later?</i>

00:03:29.337 --> 00:03:32.671
<i>Well, i'll talk to you
then. Give me a call. Thanks.</i>

00:03:37.271 --> 00:03:39.738
<i>Brock: hey, meredith, what's
going on? This is brock.</i>

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:42.571
<i>I just wanted to let you know
the gang is gonna get together.</i>

00:03:42.604 --> 00:03:44.404
<i>We're gonna go to the garage.</i>

00:03:44.437 --> 00:03:46.437
<i>We're gonna have some
beers and some shots.</i>

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:19.937
All right, dean, this is the place.

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:21.937
I've got to say dad and me did just fine

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:24.304
Without these stupid costumes.

00:04:24.337 --> 00:04:27.638
I feel like a
high-School-Drama dork.

00:04:29.504 --> 00:04:31.471
What was that play that you did?

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:33.304
What was it
-- "Our town"?

00:04:33.337 --> 00:04:34.970
Yeah, you were good. It was cute.

00:04:35.004 --> 00:04:36.803
Look, you want to pull this off or not?

00:04:36.837 --> 00:04:39.337
I'm just saying these outfits
cost hard-Earned money.

00:04:39.371 --> 00:04:40.437
Whose?

00:04:40.471 --> 00:04:43.803
Ours. You think
credit-Card fraud is easy?

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:48.037
Thanks for letting us look around.

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:51.571
The police said they were
done with the place, so...

00:05:02.204 --> 00:05:04.337
You guys said you were
with the alarm company?

00:05:04.371 --> 00:05:05.704
That's right.

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:07.004
Well, no offense,

00:05:07.037 --> 00:05:10.170
But your alarm is about as
useful as boobs on a man.

00:05:10.204 --> 00:05:12.170
Well, that's
why we're here --

00:05:12.204 --> 00:05:15.537
To see what went wrong, to
stop it from happening again.

00:05:17.571 --> 00:05:19.371
Now, ma'am, you found the body?

00:05:19.404 --> 00:05:20.537
Yeah.

00:05:20.571 --> 00:05:21.870
Right after it happened?

00:05:21.903 --> 00:05:23.204
No, a few days later.

00:05:23.237 --> 00:05:25.870
Meredith's work called.
She hadn't showed up.

00:05:25.903 --> 00:05:27.970
I knocked on her door.

00:05:28.004 --> 00:05:30.937
That's when i noticed... the smell.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:34.404
Any windows open? Any sign of break-In?

00:05:34.437 --> 00:05:35.870
Windows were locked.
Front door was bolted.

00:05:35.903 --> 00:05:38.271
Chain was on the door. We
had to cut it to get in.

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:39.604
And the alarm was still on?

00:05:39.638 --> 00:05:42.604
Like i said. Bang-Up job
your company is doing.

00:05:42.638 --> 00:05:44.704
Did you see any overturned furniture,

00:05:44.738 --> 00:05:46.371
Broken glass, signs of struggle?

00:05:46.404 --> 00:05:49.337
Everything was in perfect condition...

00:05:49.371 --> 00:05:51.271
Except meredith.

00:05:51.304 --> 00:05:54.437
Well, what condition was meredith in?

00:05:54.471 --> 00:05:57.837
Meredith was all over, in pieces.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:00.704
The guy who killed her
must have been a whack job.

00:06:00.738 --> 00:06:03.304
But i tell you, if i
didn't know any better,

00:06:03.337 --> 00:06:05.537
I'd have said a wild animal did it.

00:06:08.571 --> 00:06:11.170
Ma'am, you mind if we take some time,

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:13.271
Give this place a once-Over?

00:06:13.304 --> 00:06:16.704
Go right ahead. Knock yourself out.

00:06:22.104 --> 00:06:24.237
So the killer walks in
and out of the apartment --

00:06:24.271 --> 00:06:25.738
No weapons, no prints, nothing.

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:28.070
I'm telling you, the
minute i found that article,

00:06:28.104 --> 00:06:29.738
I knew this was our kind of gig.

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:31.271
I think i agree with you.

00:06:31.304 --> 00:06:33.770
So, you talked to the cops?

00:06:33.803 --> 00:06:37.304
Uh, yeah, i
spoke to amy --

00:06:37.337 --> 00:06:41.304
A, uh, charming, perky
officer of the law.

00:06:41.337 --> 00:06:42.638
What did you find out?

00:06:42.671 --> 00:06:45.638
Well, she's a sagittarius.
She loves tequila.

00:06:45.671 --> 00:06:47.837
I mean...whew.

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:50.004
Oh, and she's got this
little tattoo. Dean!

00:06:50.037 --> 00:06:51.170
What? Yeah.

00:06:51.204 --> 00:06:53.004
Nothing we don't already know,

00:06:53.037 --> 00:06:56.304
Except for one thing they're
keeping out of the papers.

00:06:56.337 --> 00:06:57.770
Meredith's heart was missing.

00:06:59.604 --> 00:07:00.738
Her heart?

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:03.237
Yeah, her heart.

00:07:03.271 --> 00:07:05.070
So, what do you think did it to her?

00:07:05.104 --> 00:07:07.471
The landlady said it looked
like an animal attack.

00:07:07.504 --> 00:07:10.371
Maybe it was. Werewolf?

00:07:10.404 --> 00:07:12.271
Not a werewolf. The
lunar cycle's not right.

00:07:12.304 --> 00:07:13.337
If it was a creature,

00:07:13.371 --> 00:07:15.137
It would've left some kind of trace.

00:07:15.170 --> 00:07:18.803
It was probably a spirit.

00:07:18.837 --> 00:07:20.937
Hmm.

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:24.471
See if you can find
any masking tape around.

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:49.371
Ever see that symbol before?

00:07:49.404 --> 00:07:51.837
Never.

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:53.837
Me, neither.

00:08:27.204 --> 00:08:29.504
I talked to the bartender.

00:08:29.537 --> 00:08:31.937
Did you get anything...
besides her number?

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:35.803
Dude, i'm a professional.
I'm offended that...

00:08:37.437 --> 00:08:40.037
All right.

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:42.237
You mind doing a little bit of thinking

00:08:42.271 --> 00:08:44.070
With your upstairs brain, dean?

00:08:44.104 --> 00:08:45.803
Hmm? There's nothing to find out.

00:08:45.837 --> 00:08:47.837
Meredith worked here. She waited tables.

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:50.371
Everyone here is her friend.
Everyone says she's normal.

00:08:50.404 --> 00:08:52.704
She didn't do or say anything
weird before she died.

00:08:52.738 --> 00:08:54.970
What about that symbol?
Did you find anything?

00:08:55.004 --> 00:08:56.371
Nope. Nothing.

00:08:56.404 --> 00:08:58.870
It wasn't in dad's journal
or in any of the usual books.

00:08:58.903 --> 00:09:01.638
I just have to dig a
little deeper, i guess.

00:09:01.671 --> 00:09:05.037
There was a first victim,
right, before meredith?

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:07.037
Right, yeah. His name was, uh...

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:09.070
His name was ben swardstrom.

00:09:09.104 --> 00:09:11.738
Last month he was found
mutilated in his town house.

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:14.803
Same deal. The door was
locked. The alarm was on.

00:09:14.837 --> 00:09:16.738
Is there any connection between them?

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:18.070
Nothing i could tell.

00:09:18.104 --> 00:09:20.104
Ben was a banker.
Meredith was a waitress.

00:09:20.137 --> 00:09:22.204
They never met, never
knew anyone in common.

00:09:22.237 --> 00:09:24.571
They were practically
from different worlds.

00:09:24.604 --> 00:09:26.404
So the only successful
intel we've scored

00:09:26.437 --> 00:09:29.104
Is the bartender's phone number.

00:09:30.204 --> 00:09:32.404
What?

00:09:35.437 --> 00:09:36.604
Sam?

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:46.104
Meg.

00:09:46.137 --> 00:09:47.704
Sam!

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:56.170
Sam, is that you? Oh, my gosh!

00:09:57.970 --> 00:10:00.970
What are you doing here?

00:10:01.003 --> 00:10:02.937
I'm just in town
-- Visiting friends.

00:10:04.903 --> 00:10:06.037
Where are they?

00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:08.371
Well, they're not here right now,

00:10:08.404 --> 00:10:09.970
But what about you, meg?

00:10:10.003 --> 00:10:11.838
I thought you were going to california.

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:13.170
Oh, i did.

00:10:13.204 --> 00:10:15.371
I came. I saw. I conquered.

00:10:15.404 --> 00:10:17.903
Oh, and i met
what's his name --

00:10:17.937 --> 00:10:20.404
Something michael
murray -- At a bar.

00:10:20.437 --> 00:10:21.571
Who?

00:10:21.604 --> 00:10:22.838
It doesn't matter.

00:10:22.870 --> 00:10:25.237
Anyway, the whole scene got old,

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:27.537
So i'm living here for a while.

00:10:28.771 --> 00:10:30.070
You're from chicago?

00:10:30.104 --> 00:10:33.070
No, massachusetts
-- Andover.

00:10:33.104 --> 00:10:34.637
Gosh, sam,

00:10:34.671 --> 00:10:36.838
What are the odds we'd
run into each other?

00:10:36.870 --> 00:10:38.838
I know. I thought i'd
never see you again.

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:41.104
Well, i'm glad you were wrong.

00:10:44.537 --> 00:10:46.537
Dude, cover your mouth.

00:10:46.571 --> 00:10:49.437
Yeah, i'm sorry, meg.

00:10:49.471 --> 00:10:52.671
This is, um -- This
is my brother, dean.

00:10:54.704 --> 00:10:55.903
This is dean?

00:10:55.937 --> 00:10:57.704
Yeah. So you've heard of me?

00:10:57.738 --> 00:10:59.537
Oh, yeah, i've heard of you.

00:10:59.571 --> 00:11:03.337
Nice -- The way you treat
your brother like luggage.

00:11:03.371 --> 00:11:04.671
Sorry?

00:11:04.704 --> 00:11:07.270
Why don't you let him
do what he wants to do?

00:11:07.304 --> 00:11:09.704
Stop dragging him
over god's green earth.

00:11:09.738 --> 00:11:11.903
Meg...it's all right.

00:11:14.237 --> 00:11:17.371
Okay. Awkward.

00:11:17.404 --> 00:11:20.437
I'm gonna get a drink now.

00:11:25.003 --> 00:11:26.304
Sam, i'm sorry.

00:11:26.337 --> 00:11:31.003
It's just, the way you
told me he treats you,

00:11:31.037 --> 00:11:32.870
If it were me, i'd kill him.

00:11:32.903 --> 00:11:34.404
It's all right. He means well.

00:11:34.437 --> 00:11:37.037
We should hook up while you're in town.

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:38.204
Yeah.

00:11:38.237 --> 00:11:40.237
I could show you a hell of a time.

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:41.537
That sounds great.

00:11:41.571 --> 00:11:43.537
Why don't you give me your number?

00:11:43.571 --> 00:11:46.870

312-555-0143.

00:11:46.903 --> 00:11:48.738
You know what? I never
got your last name.

00:11:48.771 --> 00:11:50.371
Masters. Masters?

00:11:50.404 --> 00:11:51.604
So you better call.

00:11:51.637 --> 00:11:53.604
Scout's honor.

00:11:53.637 --> 00:11:57.637
I hope to see you around, sam.

00:12:07.137 --> 00:12:08.437
Who the hell we he?

00:12:08.471 --> 00:12:10.437
I don't really know.
I only met her once.

00:12:10.471 --> 00:12:12.771
Meeting up with her again?

00:12:12.804 --> 00:12:16.104
I don't know, man. It's weird.

00:12:16.137 --> 00:12:18.771
What was she saying --
I treat you like luggage?

00:12:18.804 --> 00:12:20.771
Were you bitching
about me to some chick?

00:12:20.804 --> 00:12:22.104
Look, i'm sorry, dean.

00:12:22.137 --> 00:12:23.604
It was when we had that huge fight

00:12:23.637 --> 00:12:25.637
When i was in the bus stop in indiana.

00:12:25.671 --> 00:12:27.637
Is there any truth to what she's saying?

00:12:27.671 --> 00:12:29.504
Am i keeping you against your will, sam?

00:12:29.537 --> 00:12:31.437
No, of course not.
Now, would you listen?

00:12:31.471 --> 00:12:33.437
What?!

00:12:33.471 --> 00:12:35.937
I think there's something
strange going on here, dean.

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:37.571
Tell me about it. She
wasn't even into me.

00:12:37.604 --> 00:12:40.137
No, man, i mean, like
our kind of strange.

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:42.137
Maybe even a lead. Why do you say that?

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:44.937
I met meg weeks ago literally
on the side of the road.

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:47.237
Now i run into her in
some random chicago bar --

00:12:47.270 --> 00:12:48.771
The same bar where a waitress

00:12:48.804 --> 00:12:50.838
Was slaughtered by
something supernatural.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:52.804
You don't think that's
weird? It happens.

00:12:52.838 --> 00:12:54.870
Well, yeah, it happens, but not to us.

00:12:54.903 --> 00:12:56.104
Look, i could be wrong.

00:12:56.137 --> 00:12:58.471
I'm just saying there's
something about this girl

00:12:58.504 --> 00:13:00.137
That i can't quite put my finger on.

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:01.804
But i bet you'd like to.

00:13:01.838 --> 00:13:03.504
But maybe she's not a suspect.

00:13:03.537 --> 00:13:05.437
Maybe you got a thing for her, huh?

00:13:05.471 --> 00:13:08.771
You're thinking too much
with your upstairs brain, huh?

00:13:08.804 --> 00:13:10.838
Do me a favor.

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:14.037
Check and see if there's a
meg masters from massachusetts

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:16.504
And see if you can't dig
anything up on that symbol.

00:13:16.537 --> 00:13:17.970
What are you gonna do?

00:13:18.003 --> 00:13:19.771
I'm gonna watch meg.

00:13:19.804 --> 00:13:21.204
Yeah.

00:13:21.237 --> 00:13:22.771
I just want to see what's what.

00:13:22.804 --> 00:13:24.304
All right, you little pervert.

00:13:24.337 --> 00:13:26.337
I'm going. I'm going.

00:13:50.504 --> 00:13:51.804
Hey.

00:13:51.838 --> 00:13:53.704
You're lurking outside
that poor girl's apartment,

00:13:53.738 --> 00:13:55.504
Aren't you? No.

00:13:57.037 --> 00:13:58.838
Yes.

00:13:58.870 --> 00:14:00.970
You've got a funny way
of showing your affection.

00:14:01.003 --> 00:14:03.671
You find anything on her or what?

00:14:03.704 --> 00:14:05.671
There's a meg masters in
the andover phone book.

00:14:05.704 --> 00:14:07.704
I even pulled up her high-School photo.

00:14:07.738 --> 00:14:09.870
Now, look, why don't
you go knock on her door

00:14:09.903 --> 00:14:12.204
And invite her to a poetry reading

00:14:12.237 --> 00:14:14.704
Or whatever it is you do, huh?

00:14:14.738 --> 00:14:16.771
What about the symbol? Any luck?

00:14:16.804 --> 00:14:19.070
Yeah, that i did have some luck with.

00:14:19.104 --> 00:14:23.070
Turns out it's zoroastrian.

00:14:23.104 --> 00:14:25.937
Very, very old-School, like
2,000 years before christ.

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:27.437
It's a sigil for a daeva.

00:14:27.471 --> 00:14:28.903
What's a daeva?

00:14:28.937 --> 00:14:30.903
It translates to
"demon of darkness" --

00:14:30.937 --> 00:14:33.237
Zoroastrian demons, and
they're savage, animalistic,

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:37.070
Nasty attitudes -- Kind
of like demonic pit bulls.

00:14:37.104 --> 00:14:39.270
How did you figure that out?

00:14:39.304 --> 00:14:41.404
You don't have a corner on
paper chasing around here.

00:14:41.437 --> 00:14:42.870
Name the last book you read.

00:14:44.903 --> 00:14:47.371
I called dad's friend
caleb. He told me, all right.

00:14:47.404 --> 00:14:48.804
Anyway, here's the thing.

00:14:48.838 --> 00:14:51.070
These daevas, they have to be summoned.

00:14:51.104 --> 00:14:52.771
So someone's controlling it?

00:14:52.804 --> 00:14:54.270
Yeah, that's what i'm saying.

00:14:54.304 --> 00:14:56.804
And from what i gather, it's
pretty risky business, too.

00:14:56.838 --> 00:14:59.237
These suckers tend to bite
the hand that feeds them...

00:14:59.270 --> 00:15:01.771
And the arms and the torsos.

00:15:01.804 --> 00:15:02.970
What do they look like?

00:15:03.003 --> 00:15:05.137
Nobody's seen them for
a couple of millennia.

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:06.771
Summoning a demon that ancient,

00:15:06.804 --> 00:15:08.504
Someone really knows their stuff.

00:15:08.537 --> 00:15:10.371
I think we've got a
major player in town.

00:15:11.838 --> 00:15:14.471
Why don't you go give that
girl a private strip-O-Gram?

00:15:14.504 --> 00:15:16.270
<i>Bite me. Bite her.</i>

00:15:16.304 --> 00:15:18.170
Don't leave teeth marks, though.

00:15:18.204 --> 00:15:20.170
Sam? Are
you --

00:15:49.337 --> 00:15:50.704
No, no,
i'm just --

00:15:50.738 --> 00:15:52.604
Pervert!

00:15:52.637 --> 00:15:55.237
What a creep!

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:51.571
I don't think you should come

00:18:51.604 --> 00:18:54.404
Because the brothers
-- They're in town.

00:18:54.437 --> 00:18:56.104
I didn't
know that --

00:19:01.237 --> 00:19:02.537
Yes, sir.

00:19:02.571 --> 00:19:08.037
Yes, i'll be here... waiting for you.

00:20:32.337 --> 00:20:35.471
What the hell?

00:20:40.971 --> 00:20:43.603
Dude, i've got to talk to you.

00:20:43.637 --> 00:20:45.804
So, hot little meg is
summoning the daeva?

00:20:45.837 --> 00:20:48.071
It looks like she was
using that black altar

00:20:48.104 --> 00:20:49.404
To control the thing.

00:20:49.438 --> 00:20:51.737
So sammy's got a thing for the bad girl.

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:53.704
And what's the deal
with that bowl again?

00:20:53.737 --> 00:20:55.537
She was talking
into it --

00:20:55.570 --> 00:20:57.670
The way witches used to
scry into crystal balls.

00:20:57.704 --> 00:20:59.304
She was communicating with someone.

00:20:59.338 --> 00:21:01.971
With the daeva? No, you said
those things were savages.

00:21:02.004 --> 00:21:04.271
No, this was someone different,

00:21:04.304 --> 00:21:06.603
Someone who's giving her orders,

00:21:06.637 --> 00:21:09.371
Someone who's coming to that warehouse.

00:21:18.371 --> 00:21:19.503
Holy crap.

00:21:19.537 --> 00:21:20.971
What?

00:21:21.004 --> 00:21:22.971
What i was gonna tell you earlier.

00:21:23.004 --> 00:21:25.470
I pulled a favor with my

00:21:25.503 --> 00:21:27.937
Friend amy over at
the police department.

00:21:27.971 --> 00:21:30.503
Complete records of the two victims.

00:21:30.537 --> 00:21:32.237
We missed something the first time.

00:21:32.271 --> 00:21:34.904
What?

00:21:34.937 --> 00:21:38.438
The first victim
-- The old man?

00:21:38.470 --> 00:21:40.804
He spent his whole life in chicago,

00:21:40.837 --> 00:21:43.570
But look where he was
born. Lawrence, kansas.

00:21:43.603 --> 00:21:44.904
Mm-Hmm.

00:21:44.937 --> 00:21:46.804
Meredith -- The
second victim?

00:21:46.837 --> 00:21:48.637
It turns out she was adopted.

00:21:48.670 --> 00:21:50.470
And guess where she's from?

00:21:57.837 --> 00:21:58.971
Holy crap.

00:21:59.004 --> 00:22:00.304
Yeah.

00:22:00.338 --> 00:22:02.570
I mean, that is where
the demon killed mom.

00:22:04.304 --> 00:22:05.971
You think meg's tied up with the demon?

00:22:06.004 --> 00:22:08.438
I think it's a definite possibility.

00:22:08.470 --> 00:22:10.971
What's the significance of lawrence?

00:22:11.004 --> 00:22:12.637
And how do these daeva things fit in?

00:22:12.670 --> 00:22:14.971
I say we trash that
black altar, grab meg,

00:22:15.004 --> 00:22:17.737
And have ourselves a
friendly little interrogation.

00:22:17.770 --> 00:22:19.603
No, we can't. We shouldn't tip her off.

00:22:19.637 --> 00:22:21.737
We've got to stake out that warehouse.

00:22:21.770 --> 00:22:24.570
We've got to see who...or
what is showing up to meet her.

00:22:24.603 --> 00:22:25.904
I'll tell you one thing.

00:22:25.937 --> 00:22:28.603
I don't think we should do this alone.

00:22:31.004 --> 00:22:32.470
We think we've got a serious lead

00:22:32.503 --> 00:22:34.137
On the thing that killed mom.

00:22:34.171 --> 00:22:40.304
So, uh, this warehouse
-- It's 1435 west erie.

00:22:40.338 --> 00:22:41.971
Dad, if you get this,

00:22:42.004 --> 00:22:44.837
Get to chicago as soon as you can.

00:22:44.870 --> 00:22:46.503
Voice mail?

00:22:46.537 --> 00:22:47.837
Yeah.

00:22:49.037 --> 00:22:50.503
Jeez. What'd you get?

00:22:50.537 --> 00:22:53.603
I ransacked
that trunk --

00:22:53.637 --> 00:22:56.104
Holy water, y weapon
that i could think of.

00:22:56.137 --> 00:22:59.537
Exorcism rituals from about
a half-Dozen religions.

00:22:59.570 --> 00:23:02.637
I'm not sure what to expect,

00:23:02.670 --> 00:23:05.603
So i guess we should just
expect everything, huh?

00:23:13.704 --> 00:23:16.338
It's a big night.

00:23:16.371 --> 00:23:18.937
Yeah.

00:23:18.971 --> 00:23:20.237
You nervous?

00:23:20.271 --> 00:23:23.770
No. No, are you?

00:23:23.804 --> 00:23:25.971
No. No way.

00:23:34.371 --> 00:23:36.171
God, could you imagine if we actually

00:23:36.204 --> 00:23:37.870
Found that damn thing, that demon?

00:23:37.904 --> 00:23:39.971
Let's not get ahead of
ourselves, all right?

00:23:40.004 --> 00:23:44.770
I know. I'm just
saying... what if we did?

00:23:44.804 --> 00:23:47.804
What if this whole
thing was over tonight?

00:23:47.837 --> 00:23:49.971
Man, i'd sleep for a month,

00:23:50.004 --> 00:23:53.837
Go back to school,
just be a person again.

00:23:53.870 --> 00:23:55.904
You want to go back to school?

00:23:55.937 --> 00:23:58.537
Yeah, once we're done hunting the thing.

00:23:59.704 --> 00:24:02.271
Why? Is there something wrong with that?

00:24:02.304 --> 00:24:06.037
No, no, it's great. Good for you.

00:24:06.071 --> 00:24:09.637
I mean, what are you gonna
do when it's all over?

00:24:09.670 --> 00:24:11.770
It's never gonna be over.

00:24:11.804 --> 00:24:13.071
There's gonna be others.

00:24:13.104 --> 00:24:15.371
There's always gonna
be something to hunt.

00:24:15.404 --> 00:24:18.204
But there's got to be something
that you want for yourself.

00:24:18.237 --> 00:24:20.637
I don't want you to leave
the second this is over.

00:24:20.670 --> 00:24:24.537
Dude, what's your problem?

00:24:30.503 --> 00:24:33.503
Why do you think i drag
you everywhere, huh?

00:24:33.537 --> 00:24:36.737
Why do you think i came
and got you at stanford?

00:24:36.770 --> 00:24:39.004
'Cause dad was in trouble.

00:24:39.037 --> 00:24:41.670
'Cause you wanted to find
the thing that killed mom.

00:24:41.704 --> 00:24:43.837
Yes, that, but it's more than that, man.

00:24:50.371 --> 00:24:55.004
You and me
and dad --

00:24:55.037 --> 00:24:58.404
I want us to be together again.

00:25:00.371 --> 00:25:04.670
I want us to be a family again.

00:25:04.704 --> 00:25:09.371
<i>Dean, we are a family.
I'd do anything for you.</i>

00:25:09.404 --> 00:25:12.404
But things will never be
the way they were before.

00:25:18.004 --> 00:25:20.670
They could be.

00:25:24.371 --> 00:25:26.037
I don't want them to be.

00:25:30.204 --> 00:25:32.204
I'm not gonna live this life forever.

00:25:32.237 --> 00:25:35.570
Dean, when this is all over,

00:25:35.603 --> 00:25:38.837
You're gonna have to
let me go my own way.

00:26:41.603 --> 00:26:45.870
Guys. Hiding is a little bit
childish, don't you think?

00:26:45.904 --> 00:26:47.870
That didn't work out like i'd planned.

00:26:50.804 --> 00:26:50.904
Why don't you come out?

00:27:01.071 --> 00:27:04.570
Sam, i have to say,

00:27:04.603 --> 00:27:07.304
This puts a real crimp
in our relationship.

00:27:07.338 --> 00:27:09.171
Yeah, tell me about it.

00:27:09.204 --> 00:27:11.870
So, where's your little daeva friend?

00:27:11.904 --> 00:27:13.104
Around.

00:27:13.137 --> 00:27:15.770
And that shotgun's
not gonna do much good.

00:27:15.804 --> 00:27:17.704
Oh, don't worry, sweetheart.

00:27:17.737 --> 00:27:19.237
The shotgun's not for the demon.

00:27:19.271 --> 00:27:22.837
So, who is it, meg? Who's coming?

00:27:22.870 --> 00:27:24.338
Who are you waiting for?

00:27:24.371 --> 00:27:26.870
You.

00:27:57.121 --> 00:28:00.287
Hey, sam, don't take this the wrong way,

00:28:00.321 --> 00:28:03.653
But your girlfriend... is a bitch.

00:28:03.687 --> 00:28:07.854
This, the whole thing, was a trap.

00:28:09.753 --> 00:28:12.387
Running into you at the bar,

00:28:12.421 --> 00:28:16.121
Following you here, hearing
what you had to say --

00:28:16.154 --> 00:28:18.187
It was all a setup, wasn't it?

00:28:19.787 --> 00:28:21.787
And that the victims were from lawrence.

00:28:21.820 --> 00:28:23.187
It doesn't mean anything.

00:28:23.221 --> 00:28:25.820
It was just to draw you in, that's all.

00:28:25.854 --> 00:28:27.687
You killed those two people for nothing.

00:28:27.720 --> 00:28:29.987
Baby, i've killed a
lot more for a lot less.

00:28:31.887 --> 00:28:35.020
You trapped us. Good for you.

00:28:35.054 --> 00:28:37.354
It's miller time.

00:28:37.387 --> 00:28:39.187
Why don't you kill us already?

00:28:39.221 --> 00:28:42.321
Not very quick on the uptake, are we?

00:28:47.954 --> 00:28:49.620
This trap isn't for you.

00:28:53.488 --> 00:28:54.653
Dad.

00:28:55.820 --> 00:28:57.254
It's a trap for dad.

00:29:00.121 --> 00:29:02.954
Oh, sweetheart, you're
dumber than you look.

00:29:02.987 --> 00:29:06.920
'Cause even if dad was
in town, which he is not,

00:29:06.954 --> 00:29:08.920
He wouldn't walk into
something like this.

00:29:08.954 --> 00:29:10.653
He's too good.

00:29:10.687 --> 00:29:13.020
He is pretty good, i'll give you that.

00:29:18.020 --> 00:29:20.020
But you see

00:29:25.354 --> 00:29:27.154
He has one weakness.

00:29:27.187 --> 00:29:28.521
What's that?

00:29:28.554 --> 00:29:30.287
You.

00:29:31.687 --> 00:29:34.554
He lets his guard down around his boys,

00:29:34.588 --> 00:29:37.954
Lets his emotions cloud his judgment.

00:29:39.920 --> 00:29:42.720
<i>I happen to know he is in town,</i>

00:29:42.753 --> 00:29:47.488
And he'll come and try to save you.

00:29:47.521 --> 00:29:50.387
And then the daevas
will kill everybody --

00:29:50.421 --> 00:29:54.987
Nice and slow... and messy.

00:29:55.020 --> 00:29:57.321
Well, i've got news for you.

00:29:57.354 --> 00:30:00.653
It's gonna take a lot more
than some...shadow to kill him.

00:30:00.687 --> 00:30:02.854
Oh, the daevas are in the room here.

00:30:02.887 --> 00:30:04.087
They're invisible.

00:30:04.121 --> 00:30:06.454
Their shadows are just
the only part you can see.

00:30:06.488 --> 00:30:07.987
Why are you doing this, meg?

00:30:08.020 --> 00:30:10.221
What kind of deal you got
worked out here, huh...

00:30:10.254 --> 00:30:11.554
And with who?

00:30:11.588 --> 00:30:13.488
I'm doing this for the same reasons

00:30:13.521 --> 00:30:15.488
You do what
you do --

00:30:15.521 --> 00:30:17.854
Loyalty, love.

00:30:23.521 --> 00:30:25.488
Like the love you had for
mommy...and jess.Go to he

00:30:25.521 --> 00:30:29.054
Baby, i'm already there.

00:30:31.087 --> 00:30:33.221
Come on, sam.

00:30:33.254 --> 00:30:36.254
There's no need to be nasty.

00:30:40.753 --> 00:30:44.720
I think we both know...

00:30:44.753 --> 00:30:47.588
How you really feel about me.

00:30:51.020 --> 00:30:52.687
You know

00:30:54.753 --> 00:30:58.720
I saw you... watching me...

00:30:58.753 --> 00:31:02.287
Changing in my apartment.

00:31:02.321 --> 00:31:04.887
It turned you on, didn't it?

00:31:04.920 --> 00:31:06.920
Get a room, you two.

00:31:06.954 --> 00:31:08.454
I didn't mind.

00:31:08.488 --> 00:31:11.121
I liked that you were watching me.

00:31:11.154 --> 00:31:13.121
Come on, sammy,

00:31:13.154 --> 00:31:16.121
You and i can still
have a little dirty fun.

00:31:16.154 --> 00:31:18.753
You want to have fun? Go ahead, then.

00:31:18.787 --> 00:31:21.287
I'm a little tied up right now.

00:31:56.488 --> 00:31:59.454
Now, were you just trying to distract me

00:31:59.488 --> 00:32:02.620
While your brother cuts free?

00:32:02.653 --> 00:32:05.287
No.

00:32:05.321 --> 00:32:07.287
No.

00:32:07.321 --> 00:32:10.187
It was because i have a knife of my own.

00:32:12.887 --> 00:32:14.187
Sam!

00:32:14.221 --> 00:32:16.054
Get the altar.

00:32:55.720 --> 00:32:57.354
So, i guess the daevas

00:32:57.388 --> 00:32:59.687
Didn't like being bossed around.

00:32:59.720 --> 00:33:01.854
I guess not.

00:33:01.887 --> 00:33:03.187
Hey, sam?

00:33:03.221 --> 00:33:04.354
Hmm?

00:33:04.388 --> 00:33:06.354
Next time you want to get laid,

00:33:06.388 --> 00:33:10.054
Find a girl that's not
so buckets of crazy, huh?

00:33:24.854 --> 00:33:27.254
Why don't you just leave
that stuff in the car?

00:33:27.288 --> 00:33:29.587
I said it before, and
i'll say it again --

00:33:29.620 --> 00:33:32.787
Better safe than sorry.

00:33:36.354 --> 00:33:37.520
Hey!

00:33:50.420 --> 00:33:52.021
Dad.

00:33:52.054 --> 00:33:54.054
Hey, boys.

00:34:22.420 --> 00:34:23.553
Hi, sam.

00:34:23.587 --> 00:34:24.921
Hi, dad.

00:34:28.453 --> 00:34:30.754
Dad, it was a trap.

00:34:30.787 --> 00:34:34.420
I didn't know. I'm sorry.

00:34:34.453 --> 00:34:37.553
It's all right. I thought
it might have been.

00:34:37.587 --> 00:34:39.121
Were you there?

00:34:39.154 --> 00:34:43.487
I got there just in time to
see the girl take the swan dive.

00:34:43.520 --> 00:34:44.887
She was the bad guy, right?

00:34:44.921 --> 00:34:46.420
Yes, sir.Yes, sir.

00:34:46.453 --> 00:34:48.921
Good. Well, it doesn't surprise me.

00:34:48.954 --> 00:34:51.388
It's tried to stop me before.

00:34:51.453 --> 00:34:53.420
The demon has?

00:34:53.453 --> 00:34:56.754
It knows i'm close. It
knows i'm gonna kill it.

00:34:56.787 --> 00:35:00.354
Not just exorcise it
or send it back to hell,

00:35:00.388 --> 00:35:03.154
Actually kill it.

00:35:03.187 --> 00:35:04.754
How?

00:35:04.787 --> 00:35:07.854
I'm working on that.

00:35:07.887 --> 00:35:11.520
Let us come with you. We'll help.

00:35:11.553 --> 00:35:15.121
No, sam.

00:35:15.154 --> 00:35:16.187
Not yet.

00:35:16.221 --> 00:35:18.453
Listen, try to understand.

00:35:18.487 --> 00:35:20.921
This demon is a scary son of a bitch.

00:35:20.954 --> 00:35:23.587
I don't want you
caught in the crossfire.

00:35:23.620 --> 00:35:24.921
I don't want you hurt.

00:35:24.954 --> 00:35:27.087
You don't have to worry about us.

00:35:27.121 --> 00:35:28.121
Of course i do.

00:35:30.453 --> 00:35:32.453
I'm your father.

00:35:36.487 --> 00:35:40.787
Listen, sammy, the last
time we were together,

00:35:40.820 --> 00:35:42.620
We had one hell of a fight.

00:35:42.654 --> 00:35:43.787
Yes, sir.

00:35:51.654 --> 00:35:54.620
It's good to see you again.

00:35:54.654 --> 00:35:56.487
It's been a long time.

00:35:58.887 --> 00:36:00.221
Too long.

00:36:27.720 --> 00:36:29.221
No!

00:37:07.967 --> 00:37:09.834
These things are shadow demons,

00:37:09.867 --> 00:37:11.567
So let's light 'em up!

00:37:26.533 --> 00:37:27.667
Dad!

00:37:27.700 --> 00:37:28.901
Over here!

00:37:31.101 --> 00:37:33.334
Come on!

00:37:58.167 --> 00:38:00.467
All right, come on. We
don't have much time.

00:38:00.500 --> 00:38:02.967
As soon as the flare's
out, they'll be back.

00:38:03.001 --> 00:38:04.533
Wait, wait!

00:38:04.567 --> 00:38:06.934
Sam, wait.

00:38:10.567 --> 00:38:12.034
Dad, you can't come with us.

00:38:12.067 --> 00:38:17.268
What? What are you talking about?

00:38:17.301 --> 00:38:18.800
We'll be all right.

00:38:18.834 --> 00:38:21.600
Dean, we should stick together!
We'll go after those --

00:38:21.634 --> 00:38:22.967
Sam, listen to me!

00:38:25.901 --> 00:38:27.934
We almost got dad killed in there.

00:38:27.967 --> 00:38:30.934
Don't you understand?
They're not gonna stop.

00:38:30.967 --> 00:38:32.533
They're gonna try again.

00:38:32.567 --> 00:38:34.967
They're gonna use us to get to him.

00:38:35.001 --> 00:38:36.667
I mean, meg was right.

00:38:36.700 --> 00:38:39.500
Dad's vulnerable when he's with us.

00:38:41.101 --> 00:38:45.500
He...he's stronger without us around.

00:38:47.567 --> 00:38:49.234
Dad...

00:38:50.934 --> 00:38:52.901
No.

00:38:52.934 --> 00:38:55.034
After everything,

00:38:55.067 --> 00:38:57.800
After all the time we
spent looking for you,

00:38:57.834 --> 00:39:00.334
Please.

00:39:00.368 --> 00:39:02.101
I've got to be a part of this fight.

00:39:02.134 --> 00:39:04.101
Sammy, this fight is just starting,

00:39:04.134 --> 00:39:06.834
And we are all gonna
have a part to play.

00:39:06.867 --> 00:39:08.600
For now, you've got to trust me, son.

00:39:10.967 --> 00:39:14.901
Okay? You've got to let me go.

00:39:58.734 --> 00:40:00.867
Be careful, boys.

00:40:02.167 --> 00:40:04.001
Come on.



00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.000
